WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.920
In this video, you will get the SoCal Lights app on your iPhone, and see what is the same as the website, and what is different.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.140
On an Android phone, you can still add the website to your home screen.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.080
On your iPhone, open the App Store.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.400
Search for SoCal Lights, and tap Get.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.140
When it finishes, tap Open.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:20.860
This is the app.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:27.160
It opens on the same map as the website, with the same places, filters, favorites and routes.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.800
And every update to the website reaches the app by itself.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.300
To sign in, tap the person icon at the top.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.360
Then tap Sign in.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.280
In the app, you sign in with a code that we email to you.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.680
You type your email, and we send the code.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.020
There is no password.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.240
Let us close this.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.940
Now tap the three dots, at the top right.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.520
Look at this menu.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.640
There is no Support item and no Feature your event.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:05.500
Tips, Featured placements and contest passes are paid on the website, so the app never asks you for a payment.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:11.080
And if you ever want to leave, open Your profile, then Account, and tap Delete my account.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.460
It takes two taps, and it removes your account and personal data.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.740
On an Android phone, use Chrome.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.460
Tap the three dots in Chrome itself, at the top of the browser, not on the site.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.700
Then tap Install app, or Add to Home screen.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.660
Next up: Find contests.

